2026-09-08 checkpoint: frontend layouts plus download/preview/live-status repairs.
Validation is synthetic only; no weights downloaded, models loaded, inference run,
production server restarted or performance benchmark claimed. Full process-restart
job durability and the broader timeout/output-limit audit remain open above.

Scope: arbitrary downloaded weights need matching runtime adapters. Unsupported
and incomplete models must remain visibly distinct from usable ones. Metadata
readiness is not a guarantee of GPU fit or generation quality.

## Requested for the production redesign — September 23

- [ ] Build an optional, small floating hardware monitor. Unsloth Studio's
      monitor is the interaction reference: open/close, drag and resize inside
      the viewport, keep its position on resize, and poll only while visible
      (its implementation polls every 5 seconds). Its current floating panel
      shows RAM and VRAM used/total with clear GiB units, usage bars, separate
      GPU pools when needed, and unknown values rather than fabricated zeroes.
      Reference: https://github.com/unslothai/unsloth/blob/main/studio/frontend/src/components/floating-monitor.tsx
- [ ] Extend DuckPond's monitor beyond that reference: CPU load and temperature,
      GPU load/temperature/VRAM, RAM and swap, SSD used/free and disk activity;
      show SSD temperature, fan speed and GPU power only where the host exposes
      reliable sensors. Allow each person to choose, reorder and hide readings,
      choose compact/expanded layout and refresh interval, and save position and
      preferences. Explain what every value means in plain-language tooltips.
      Label dedicated versus shared VRAM and GiB versus GB accurately. Read
      metrics through an authenticated server endpoint, bound polling and
      history, and show "unavailable" for unsupported sensors. Keep the panel
      clear of chat controls and usable on phones.
- [ ] Use flat colors throughout DuckPond. Remove built-in gradients from
      backgrounds, themes, cards, loading states, weather cards, login, voice
      controls, and mascot framing; do not introduce new gradients.
- [ ] Push reviewed implementation checkpoints to GitHub and update main
      periodically after the build and release review. Keep the live auto-deploy
      source protected from partial work; record the commit and deployment state.


